  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 245 AM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nThursday through Monday...If the currently extrapolated short wave \ntrain along the edge of the heat dome is in the ballpark, we may \nhave another MCS moving into the local area Thu morning with severe \nweather and heavy rain risks. The temperature battle will continue \nas well with LLVL baroclinicity and thermal ribbon wavering acrs the \nregion for high heat or not so bad depending on the daily flux. \nRainfall amounts may really add up by the weekend and early next \nweek on the northern fringe of the heat dome from the west central \nplains, acrs IA/IL, and curving down acrs the eastern OH RVR Valley. \nWill have to watch the Thu through Friday period for heavy rain and \nback building MCS potential depending on LLVL boundary and \nconvergent flow axis's lay out if long range 2 inch PWAT feed \nindicators are accurate.",
